# Segment Page Conventions

When creating, editing, or auditing segment pages in `content/segments/`:

## 1. Mandatory Segment Picture
Every segment page MUST include an authentic screencap picture directly beneath the primary `# Segment Name` heading:

```markdown
# Segment Name

![Segment Name on Barely Informed News](https://github.com/trak3r/binlore/releases/download/media-assets/<segment-slug>.jpg)
```

### Screencap Extraction & Upload Workflow:
1. Extract a clear frame showing the segment's title card, transition screen, or in-segment action from its VOD appearance using `tools/binlore_tools/screencap.py` via `ffmpeg`.
2. Save the screencap locally to `tools/screencaps/<segment-slug>.jpg`.
3. Upload the asset to GitHub release `media-assets` on repository `trak3r/binlore`:
 ```bash
 gh release upload media-assets --repo trak3r/binlore tools/screencaps/<segment-slug>.jpg --clobber
 ```
4. Embed the URL `https://github.com/trak3r/binlore/releases/download/media-assets/<segment-slug>.jpg` right under the `# Segment Name` heading.

## 2. Required Structure & Cross-Links
- Frontmatter (`title`, `type: segment`, `aliases`, `status`, `tags: [segment, ...]`).
- `# Name` + Image embed directly under heading.
- Format & Overview.
- Key Elements, Hosts, Recurring Tropes, or Lore.
- Cross-links to hosts, correspondents, and relevant storylines.
- Always add/update the segment's entry in `content/segments/index.md`.
